            <ArticleTitle>Follow-up of the Finnish Asthma Programme 2000-2010: reduction of hospital burden needs risk group rethinking.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>292-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/thoraxjnl-2011-201028</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Finnish Asthma Programme 1994-2004 focused on early intervention and disease control, thereby resulting in a significant reduction of asthma morbidity. During the follow-up period from 2000 to 2010, the number of hospital days continued to fall by 54%. Patients ≥65 years, especially women, accounted for 39% of the hospital days, and they need attention if the hospital burden is to be reduced further.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
